# portability-guard.allow — darwin-mac-ops (smDrainDesk-08, 2026-09-07)
# The guard reads THIS file from the repo it is committing in (cd toplevel; ALLOW=portability-guard.allow),
# not ~/Scripts', so the `*.plist` allowance over there never applied here. That went unnoticed
# until core.hooksPath became global on 2026-09-07 and the first new plist after it was refused.
# Format: <glob> | <why this one is deliberately darwin-only>
*.plist                     | launchd. macOS-only by construction (launchd does not expand ~); feynman schedules with systemd.
launchagents/*              | ditto — these are darwin's limbs, not portable tools.
# retired-plists/* was copied over from ~/Scripts's allowlist and retired 2026-09-07
# by feynmanSync-08: this repo tracks no such directory, so the line excused nothing
# while reading as a deliberate ruling. Re-add it the day this repo grows one.
